<title>FRANCE: Firefighters put out ship blaze in Channel.</title>
<headline>Firefighters put out ship blaze in Channel.</headline>
<dateline>RENNES, France 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>French and British firemen dropped from helicopters and put out a fire aboard a Danish freighter off the Channel island of Guernsey on Friday, rescue services said.</p>
<p>They said the freighter Danica Sunrise, bound for Rotterdam from Malaga with five people on board and a cargo of stones, suffered slight damage and should resume its route shortly.</p>
</text>
